        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7960aeae-7f61-560b-a4e3-16a7229ed7c0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Ghana, Elubo, Sekondi-Takoradi, Cape Coast, Winneba, Accra, Tema, Aflao\n- Systems: N1, National Highway 1\n- Events: Fancy Dress Festival, Kakamotobi\n- Topics: fishing ports, masquerade festivals\n\nFacts:\n- The N1, or National Highway 1, is a national highway in Ghana that begins at Elubo on the Ivory Coast border and ends at Aflao on the Togo border.\n- The N1 passes through Sekondi-Takoradi, Cape Coast, Winneba, Accra, and Tema.\n- Winneba, traditionally known as Simpa, is a historic fishing port on the south coast of Ghana.\n- Winneba lies 90 miles east of Cape Coast.\n- The Fancy Dress Festival, locally called Kakamotobi, is a masquerade festival celebrated by the people of Winneba in Ghana's Central Region.\n- The Fancy Dress Festival is held every year from Christmas to the first day of January.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "2fc5f898-351d-5dad-b44d-4e5931e77718",
        "text": "Page: N1 road (Ghana). Sentence: The N1 or National Highway 1 is a national highway in Ghana that begins at the border with Ivory Coast at Elubo and runs through Sekondi-Takoradi, Cape Coast, Winneba, Accra and Tema to the border with Togo at Aflao.\nPage: Winneba. Sentence: Winneba, traditionally known as \"Simpa\", is a historic fishing port in south Ghana, lying on the south coast, 90 mi east of Cape Coast.\nPage: Fancy Dress Festival. Sentence: The Fancy Dress Festival(known locally as \"Kakamotobi\") is a masquerade festival held on Christmas to the first day of January every year by the people of Winneba in the Central region of Ghana.",
